{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791104799,"nonce":"FnydFMNfZTd9rwjks/nrcjGxThM=","title":"A restyle that sets an equal value starts a tween that moves nowhere","message":"Found by the motion recorder: hovering a Button starts seven transitions; one (background) changes, the other six (color, four border colours, shadow) go from a value to the same value and still run their full 180ms, so the frame loop keeps drawing and the trace fills with no-op tracks. MotionCheck now flags these as \"moved nowhere: from equals to\".\n\nCause: Tweened.retarget returns early only on `value == to`, a reference comparison; a restyle builds new Color/Brush/Shadow/Transform objects equal in value to the current ones. Compare by value for the property's type (rgb and alpha; a solid brush's colour; shadow layers; transform fields) before starting a move.","files":null}]}